# Code Conventions

## Naming Conventions

| Type       | Python          | TypeScript/JavaScript | MDX              |
| ---------- | --------------- | --------------------- | ---------------- |
| Files      | `snake_case.py` | `kebab-case.ts`       | `kebab-case.mdx` |
| Functions  | `snake_case`    | `camelCase`           | N/A              |
| Classes    | `PascalCase`    | `PascalCase`          | N/A              |
| Constants  | `UPPER_SNAKE`   | `UPPER_SNAKE`         | N/A              |
| Components | N/A             | `PascalCase.tsx`      | N/A              |
| Docs       | N/A             | N/A                   | `kebab-case.mdx` |

## Code Style

- **Python**: Follow PEP 8, use type hints, docstrings for public APIs
- **TypeScript**: Strict mode enabled, no `any` types, use interfaces
- **JavaScript**: ESLint + Prettier, prefer `const` over `let`
- **MDX**: Use frontmatter, proper heading hierarchy, code blocks with language tags

## File Organization

- One component/class per file
- Group related files in feature directories
- Keep test files adjacent to source files or in `tests/` directory
- Documentation files (*.mdx) in `docs/` or `src/content/docs/` directories
